# Title: Potential Suspicious Change To Sensitive/Critical Files
# ID: 86157017-c2b1-4d4a-8c33-93b8e67e4af4
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: @d4ns4n_ (Wuerth-Phoenix)
# Date: 2023-05-30
# Tags: attack.impact, attack.t1565.001
# Description: Detects changes of sensitive and critical files. Monitors files that you don't expect to change without planning on Linux system.
# These files include, but are not limited to, system configuration files, authentication files, and critical application files.
# Attackers often target these files to maintain persistence, escalate privileges, or disrupt system operations.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((process.executable:*/cat OR process.executable:*/echo OR process.executable:*/grep OR process.executable:*/head OR process.executable:*/more OR process.executable:*/tail) AND process.command_line:*>*) OR ((process.executable:*/emacs OR process.executable:*/nano OR process.executable:*/sed OR process.executable:*/vi OR process.executable:*/vim))) AND ((process.command_line:*/bin/login* OR process.command_line:*/bin/passwd* OR process.command_line:*/boot/* OR process.command_line:*/etc/*.conf* OR process.command_line:*/etc/cron.* OR process.command_line:*/etc/crontab* OR process.command_line:*/etc/hosts* OR process.command_line:*/etc/init.d* OR process.command_line:*/etc/sudoers* OR process.command_line:*/opt/bin/* OR process.command_line:*/sbin* OR process.command_line:*/usr/bin/* OR process.command_line:*/usr/local/bin/*)) AND NOT (1=1))
